  "question": {
    "text": "When benzene sulphonic acid and $p$-nitrophenol are treated with $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$, the gases released respectively are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "g6x8U",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SO}_2, \\mathrm{NO}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dU8nW",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SO}_2, \\mathrm{NO}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FCqmO",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SO}_2, \\mathrm{CO}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wWWkM",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{CO}_2, \\mathrm{CO}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Benzene sulphonic acid and p-nitrophenol react with } \\mathrm{NaHCO}_3 \\text { and evolve } \\mathrm{CO}_2 \\text { gas. }\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/VYAE7Q7eQIqgFrITxHedCdwWvz6pLzQ0SOd5pTlVftE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nBecause benezene sulphonic acid and $p$-nitro phenol are stronger acids with $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$ (i.e., $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{CO}_2$ ) so, they are capable to evolve $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ with $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$.\n$$\n\\mathrm{HCO}_3^{-}+\\underset{\\text { Acid }}{\\mathrm{H}^{+}} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{CO}_2 \\uparrow\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
